  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "H9HakaFa+kP1eFGXjCxAXkEWEw4=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-16T20:32:40.813Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## Claim\n\nSandboxes, permission prompts, and filters are preventative. They cannot answer post-hoc questions such as which skill exfiltrated data or whether provenance matches access policy.\n\nA signed operation log carrying actor, skill, inputs read, and state written makes those questions decidable. Compromised or divergent skill versions leave detectable traces against expected reducer output.\n\n## Co-signing\n\nHigh-stakes workflows can co-sign actions with input state hash or previous operation ID so swapped context between dispatch and execution fails to apply.\n\n## Scope of claim\n\nProvenance does not prevent attacks; it makes them attributable so defense is not guesswork.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-16T20:32:40.813Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-16T20:32:40.813Z"
    }
  },
